        "decision": "accept",
        "reason": "Bit-exact equivalence verified: the multiplier 0x02040810 spreads a masked nibble to bit positions {4,11,18,25}+{0..3} with all 16 contribution positions pairwise distinct, so the product is a carry-free OR; masking with 0x10101010 yields exactly b0->4, b1->12, b2->20, b3->28, matching the original vi0 insertions, and (qhi>>16)&0xF reproduces the vi1 mapping of qh bits 16-19. The hoisted scalar vh = qh>>(4*iqs) with qhi = vh>>(4*i) reproduces the original qh>>(4*(iqs+i)). Sign-extension exposure is identical to the original for the reachable iqs+i<=3 range, and the masked multiply peaks near 5.07e8, inside signed-int range with no overflow. The impl signature change (int* to int&) is contained: the only caller in the declared file is vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1, updated consistently; any external caller would fail at compile rather than silently miscompute. Governance: arithmetic change class inside sealed cuda-vecdotq-v1 authority with declared files/symbols matching the allowed set; no wave-count or launch-geometry change, so no collision with dnr-q5-four-wave or any other DNR fingerprint; spends the single open claim-authorized hypothesis akh-v2-q5-type-specific-dequant with the stated falsifier carried verbatim; expected_dispatch reproduces exactly the three sealed true/true anchors (6063/57344, 4644/8192, 3096/311296) and correctly excludes the 129-call false/true tail; cold_serialized load mode matches the fallback-only admission profile. Performance: trades ~8 dependent shift/and/or ops per element for one v_mul_lo_u32 plus masks; integer multiply is slower per-issue on gfx90a, so the win is not guaranteed, but it is a plausible VALU-pressure reduction and the governed exact-kernel-plus-graphs-on screen is the correct instrument to decide it. Correctness-preserving, in-scope, novel versus the DNR corpus: accept for measurement."
