        "reason": "Accept. The patch stays exactly within cuda-vecdotq-v1 authority (declared file ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vecdotq.cuh; declared symbols vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1 and vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1_impl) and is a genuine Q5_0-type-specific arithmetic mechanism consistent with hypothesis akh-v2-q5-type-specific-dequant. Correctness: (1) the wrapper change hoists the loop-invariant qh word and replaces per-iteration shifts `>> (4*(iqs+i))` with `(qh >> 4*iqs) >> (4*i)`, which is bitwise-identical for arithmetic shifts since total shift <= 12 bits (iqs in {0,2}, vdr=2, QI5_0=4); downstream masking in the impl is unchanged. (2) The FAST_FP16_AVAILABLE epilogue rewrites d5*(sumi*ds8.x - c*ds8.y) as sumi*(d5*ds8).x - c*(d5*ds8).y with the products fused via __hmul2; algebraically equivalent, and the float->half conversion of d5 is lossless because d5 originates as the half bq5_0->d. The only numeric delta is half-precision rounding of the scale products, which is the exact idiom already present in this file for Q4_0/Q4_1 (the sealed preimage excerpt shows vec_dot_q4_1_q8_1_impl using __half22float2(__hmul2(dm4, ds8)) under the same guard), so the 1139-case MUL_MAT suite tolerance already covers this behavior for sibling types; the #else branch preserves the original float path. FAST_FP16_AVAILABLE is active on gfx90a (V_PK_MUL_F16), so the new path is exercised on target. Governance: no launch-geometry, wave-count, workgroup, LDS, or kernel-identity change, so the three declared true/true anchors (6063/57344, 4644/8192, 3096/311296, wg=128, lds=1024) are the correct expected dispatch; the 129-call false/true tail is properly omitted per the template's explicit planner_target_exclusion, and no MMQ q5_0 geometry is resident in this frame. No DNR collision: dnr-q5-four-wave is launch geometry in mmvq.cu, dnr-q8-fp-dequant-port covers Q8_0, and this is neither. cold_serialized load mode correctly follows the fallback-only admission policy. Falsifier matches the portfolio's primary falsifier. Diff hunk line counts are well-formed against the sealed preimage (source sha c418082b... matches the template's production_instrument_target_sha256). Reservation (non-blocking): expected effect is small \u2014 the compiler likely already CSEs the redundant qh load in the unrolled loop, and the fused half multiply saves only ~1-2 VALU ops per vec_dot call \u2014 so this may land below the 0.5% nomination floor; but with the type-6 band at 27.43% of graphs-off device time, the mechanism is plausible, correctness-preserving, and cheap to screen under the governed conjunction (exact-kernel duration gain plus graphs-on whole-model gain), which is precisely what the candidate budget of 3 is for."
